---
import Motto from "../../components/Motto.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Linux Foundations is a hands-on course for anyone who wants to understand, build, and repair the computers they use. Learn with live sessions and a private AI guide."
    />
    <title>Linux Foundations | Kolam Ayer Makers</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Kolam Ayer Makers home">
        <img src="/kolam-makers-logo.png" alt="Kolam Ayer Makers" />
        <Motto compact />
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="/learn/linux-foundations/" aria-current="page">Linux Foundations</a>
        <a href="/#next">What's next</a>
        <a href="/#contact">Get involved</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <p class="terminal-line"><span>student@laptop</span>:<b>~</b>$ learn --by-doing</p>
          <h1 id="hero-heading">Understand your computer.<br /><em>Build with it.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">
            Linux Foundations is a practical course in using a computer as a tool you can understand,
            direct, and repair. Build real things on Linux, with people in the room and an AI guide
            between sessions.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/#contact">Join the next build <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></a>
            <a class="button" href="#how">How it works</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="poster">
          <img
            src="/linux-foundations-poster.png"
            alt="Linux Foundations, a free Kolam Ayer Makers course on mastering the Linux command line"
          />
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="manifesto" aria-label="Linux Foundations outcomes">
        <p>Understand the system.</p>
        <p>Make useful things.</p>
        <p>Keep learning.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="for-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / no gatekeeping</p>
        <h2 id="for-heading">For anyone who wants to learn.</h2>
        <div class="two-column">
          <p>
            This is for complete beginners, students, developers, engineers, returning tinkerers,
            and curious people. You do not need prior Linux experience. You need curiosity and a
            willingness to try.
          </p>
          <p>
            Different people arrive for different reasons: to understand their computer better,
            work confidently in a development environment, return to an old interest, or build the
            next strange project. The foundations are the same.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="panel-section" aria-labelledby="learn-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / learn the machine</p>
        <h2 id="learn-heading">Skills that compound.</h2>
        <div class="skills">
          <article>
            <h3>Use Linux</h3>
            <p>Navigate the shell, work with files, use SSH, understand permissions, and read what the system tells you.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Build and publish</h3>
            <p>Keep your work in Git, write shell scripts, and publish a personal website from source you own.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Run and repair</h3>
            <p>Trace network and HTTP problems, inspect logs, run a user service, automate routine work, and recover from mistakes.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-copy">
          Linux is a foundation for programming, web development, self-hosting, engineering work,
          creative projects, automation, and ideas nobody has thought of yet. The aim is not to
          memorise commands. It is to become someone who can keep learning.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="how" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / live, practical, supported</p>
        <h2 id="how-heading">Learn by doing. Not watching.</h2>
        <div class="two-column">
          <p>
            The course combines hands-on sessions with self-study guides, recaps, and optional
            reinforcement quests. Bring a laptop, type commands, make safe mistakes, ask questions,
            and fix problems with other people.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each released session gives you focused work. Catch up on unfinished work, go deeper
            when you are ready, and use the supporting material between sessions. The next lesson
            is still a shared part of the journey, not something you rush through alone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide" aria-labelledby="guide-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / help when you need it</p>
        <h2 id="guide-heading">A private AI guide,<br /><em>built into the course.</em></h2>
        <div class="guide-grid">
          <div>
            <p>
              <code>guide</code> is an AI tutor available in your terminal and through IRC direct
              messages. It knows the session you have reached, the commands you have learned, your
              current objective, and the course documentation that applies.
            </p>
            <p>
              It starts with useful questions and nudges, points you to the right material, and
              helps you choose what to try next. You can get unstuck without waiting for the next
              session, while still doing the thinking and building yourself.
            </p>
          </div>
          <aside>
            <p class="prompt">classroom:~$ <span>guide now</span></p>
            <p>The guide can explain and coach. It cannot edit your files, run your commands, award progress, or do the work for you.</p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="proof-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">05 / make it real</p>
        <h2 id="proof-heading">Leave with proof.</h2>
        <div class="two-column">
          <p>
            You will build a live personal site, its source repository, reusable scripts,
            documentation, and a service you can explain, inspect, and recover.
          </p>
          <p>
            Progress comes from evidence: commands you ran, files you made, services you operated,
            and explanations you can give. The AI helps you learn. The course checks the work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="clone" aria-labelledby="clone-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 / copy, improve, repeat</p>
        <h2 id="clone-heading">Build this where you are.</h2>
        <p>
          Kolam Ayer Makers began at Kolam Ayer Community Club, but it should not stay there. Want
          to run a free maker class in your own community? We need volunteers, mentors, and fellow
          makers to help clone the work.
        </p>
        <a class="button primary" href="/#contact">Get involved <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <Motto />
      <a href="https://github.com/KolamAyerMakers/monorepo">GitHub</a>
      <p>Made in Singapore &lt;3</p>
    </footer>

    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: dark; --ink: #e8e8dd; --muted: #9ca49d; --lime: #c5f414; --teal: #00e0d0; --orange: #ff725c; --panel: #111613; --line: #2b3b35; --black: #090c0a; }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body { background: var(--black); color: var(--ink); font-family: "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, "Liberation Mono", Menlo, monospace; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; }
      body::before { background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0, 224, 208, .035) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0, 224, 208, .035) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 32px 32px; content: ""; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; position: fixed; z-index: -1; }
      a { color: inherit; }
      .site-header { align-items: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin: auto; max-width: 1240px; padding: 1rem 2rem; }
      .brand { display: flex; flex-direction: column; text-decoration: none; width: min(19rem, 36vw); }
      .brand img { display: block; height: auto; width: 100%; }
      nav { display: flex; gap: clamp(.75rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); }
      nav a { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; text-decoration: none; text-transform: uppercase; }
      nav a:hover, nav a:focus-visible, nav a[aria-current="page"] { color: var(--lime); }
      main { margin: auto; max-width: 1240px; }
      section { padding: clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 9rem) 2rem; }
      .hero { align-items: center; display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(16rem, .7fr); padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem); padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
      .terminal-line, .prompt { color: var(--teal); font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: lowercase; }
      .eyebrow { color: var(--teal); font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .terminal-line span, .prompt span { color: var(--lime); }
      .terminal-line b { color: var(--orange); }
      h1, h2, h3, p { margin-top: 0; }
      h1, h2 { font-family: Impact, Haettenschweiler, "Arial Narrow Bold", sans-serif; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -.05em; line-height: .87; text-transform: uppercase; }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 5.3rem); margin: 1.1rem 0 1.5rem; }
      h2 { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 5.5rem); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
      h1 em, h2 em { color: var(--lime); font-style: normal; }
      h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.1; }
      .hero-copy, .two-column p, .section-copy, .clone > p { color: var(--muted); font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.2rem); max-width: 45rem; }
      .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
      .button { border: 1px solid var(--teal); color: var(--teal); display: inline-block; font-size: .85rem; padding: .9rem 1rem; text-decoration: none; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .button:hover, .button:focus-visible { background: var(--teal); color: var(--black); }
      .button.primary { background: var(--lime); border-color: var(--lime); color: var(--black); font-weight: bold; }
      .button.primary:hover, .button.primary:focus-visible { background: var(--orange); border-color: var(--orange); }
      .poster { border: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; padding: .75rem; }
      .poster img { display: block; height: auto; width: 100%; }
      .manifesto { background: var(--lime); color: var(--black); display: grid; font-family: Impact, Haettenschweiler, "Arial Narrow Bold", sans-serif; font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 2.1rem); grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1; padding-bottom: 1.8rem; padding-top: 1.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .manifesto p { margin: 0; }
      .two-column, .guide-grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem); grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .panel-section, .guide, .clone { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .skills { display: grid; gap: 1px; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
      .skills article { background: var(--panel); padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
      .skills p, .guide-grid p { color: var(--muted); }
      .guide { background: var(--panel); }
      .guide aside { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
      code { color: var(--lime); font: inherit; }
      .clone { background: var(--lime); color: var(--black); }
      .clone .eyebrow, .clone > p { color: var(--black); }
      .clone .button { background: var(--black); border-color: var(--black); color: var(--lime); }
      .clone .button:hover, .clone .button:focus-visible { background: var(--teal); border-color: var(--teal); color: var(--black); }
      footer { color: var(--muted); display: flex; font-size: .75rem; justify-content: space-between; margin: auto; max-width: 1240px; padding: 2rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
      @media (max-width: 700px) { .site-header { padding: .75rem 1rem; } nav { gap: .75rem; } nav a { font-size: .62rem; } section { padding-left: 1rem; padding-right: 1rem; } .manifesto, .two-column, .guide-grid, .skills { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .manifesto { gap: .75rem; } footer { display: block; padding: 1.5rem 1rem; } }
      @media (max-width: 480px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
